# bv (beads viewer) local config and caches
.bv/

# .beads/* rather than .beads/, so that the one tracked file in there can be
# re-included below.  bd stages .beads/issues.jsonl itself after every
# mutating command, and `git add` refuses any path underneath an ignored
# *directory* -- even a tracked one, and even when the file itself matches no
# ignore rule.  With the directory ignored, every bd command ended in
# "Warning: auto-export: git add failed: exit status 1" and the export had to
# be staged by hand with `git add -u`.  Ignoring the contents instead leaves
# the directory visible, so the negation works and bd stages cleanly.
# Everything else under .beads/ (the Dolt database, server pid/log/port
# files, ephemeral sqlite, backups) stays ignored by the glob.
.beads/*
!.beads/issues.jsonl
/capture.rdc

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
/image4.png

# The Hexen II demo tarball is fetched, not committed: 13 MB of binary, and we
# have no right to redistribute it -- the only licence shipped with it is
# Activision's retail EULA, which forbids distributing copies (uhexen2-3vmk).
# Users fetch it themselves via scripts/get_demo.sh / .cmd.  See
# assets/demo/README.md for the source URL, sha256 and the full reasoning.
/assets/demo/hexen2demo_nov1997-linux-i586.tgz
